[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5650635623","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123458#issuecomment-5650635623","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123458","id":5650635623,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABUM3bZw","user":{"login":"EdwardChanCH","id":97891482,"node_id":"U_kgDOBdW0mg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97891482?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH","html_url":"https://github.com/EdwardChanCH","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-13T03:14:18Z","updated_at":"2026-09-13T03:15:28Z","body":"See also https://chat.godotengine.org/channel/documentation?msg=jGxkdiDvYhcZA96JE from 2026, quote:\r\n\r\n> It just dawned on me that its advice applies much more strongly to the class reference than the rest of the manual. The manual benefits from this rule much less if followed strictly... and because the docs use it so often someone later added \"(sometimes)\" in parentheses next to the \"However\" in the list which is so sad.\r\n> \r\n> I personally avoid \"but\", \"however\", etc. because indeed, it tends to ruin the flow of a sentence in the class reference. It's very confusing to state something, then say \"but wait, there's an exception here\". And yet that happens all the time.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5650635623/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5652643371","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123458#issuecomment-5652643371","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123458","id":5652643371,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABUOx-Kw","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-13T10:13:22Z","updated_at":"2026-09-13T10:13:45Z","body":"No, I'd be hesitant to approve this PR. Oxford commas are a very low-priority issue that is generally tackled \"while we're at it\". Although I'm personally more lax on this aspect than others, this PR would cause a lot of translations to be invalidated, with very little benefit and for a difference that is very hard to spot, especially on huge walls of text.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5652643371/reactions","total_count":6,"+1":2,"-1":2,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":2,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5655000936","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123458#issuecomment-5655000936","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123458","id":5655000936,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABURB3aA","user":{"login":"JimmyCushnie","id":32693298,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNjkzMjk4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32693298?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JimmyCushnie","html_url":"https://github.com/JimmyCushnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JimmyCushnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JimmyCushnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JimmyCushnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JimmyCushnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JimmyCushnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JimmyCushnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JimmyCushnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JimmyCushnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JimmyCushnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-13T17:51:26Z","updated_at":"2026-09-13T17:51:26Z","body":"That makes sense.\r\n\r\nI forgot about this until your comment, but my previous PR #101864 was also not merged because its very minor change would invalidate translations. For that reason I haven't bothered to PR fixes for many other examples of clunky phrasing that I've since encountered in the docs.\r\n\r\nIt seems to me like this translation invalidation holds the docs back from receiving polish and cleanup that would improve them. I haven't done any serious translation work myself so I might be missing something, but I don't think minor style fixes that don't change the meaning of the text should invalidate translations. Has there been any discussion about providing a way to skip the invalidation where appropriate? Maybe we could make it so that if a PR has a certain tag, its changes do not invalidate translations?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5655000936/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5655268212","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123458#issuecomment-5655268212","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123458","id":5655268212,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABURSLdA","user":{"login":"DeanLemans","id":111811264,"node_id":"U_kgDOBqoawA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/111811264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeanLemans","html_url":"https://github.com/DeanLemans","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeanLemans/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeanLemans/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeanLemans/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeanLemans/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeanLemans/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeanLemans/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeanLemans/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeanLemans/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeanLemans/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-13T18:38:11Z","updated_at":"2026-09-13T18:38:11Z","body":"wel doesnt that mean the earlier its merged in the better? were still in dev release right? isnt the point of that \"breaking\" stuff? if we wait longer to merge it then will cause bigger pain in the future.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5655268212/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5655290362","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123458#issuecomment-5655290362","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123458","id":5655290362,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABURTh-g","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-13T18:42:01Z","updated_at":"2026-09-13T18:42:01Z","body":"The current system does not allow us to be selective because Git is not considered at all, only the difference between old and new docs. But there's so much room from improvement that is vaguely discussed occasionally, yet no concrete implementation in sight.\r\n\r\n> wel doesnt that mean the earlier its merged in the better? were still in dev release right? isnt the point of that \"breaking\" stuff? if we wait longer to merge it then will cause bigger pain in the future.\r\n\r\nAgain, commas are generally fixed \"while we're at it\". Many of the affected description could definitely use touch-ups that would be way more meaningful than adding commas, as @JimmyCushnie happened to have noticed as well:\r\n\r\n> While making this PR I noticed a few small issues with the docs that are not strictly missing commas, but which occur around missing commas","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5655290362/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5655862905","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123458#issuecomment-5655862905","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123458","id":5655862905,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABUR2eeQ","user":{"login":"JimmyCushnie","id":32693298,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNjkzMjk4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32693298?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JimmyCushnie","html_url":"https://github.com/JimmyCushnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JimmyCushnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JimmyCushnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JimmyCushnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JimmyCushnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JimmyCushnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JimmyCushnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JimmyCushnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JimmyCushnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JimmyCushnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-13T20:20:08Z","updated_at":"2026-09-13T20:20:08Z","body":"> The current system does not allow us to be selective because Git is not considered at all, only the difference between old and new docs. But there's so much room from improvement that is vaguely discussed occasionally, yet no concrete implementation in sight.\r\n\r\nOkay. When I have some time I'll work on a concrete/actionable proposal for this.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5655862905/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5661330287","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123458#issuecomment-5661330287","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123458","id":5661330287,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABUXELbw","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-14T08:42:46Z","updated_at":"2026-09-14T16:57:44Z","body":"As much as tend to do broad proofreading changes of nitpicky varieties I don't think I can accept this change without a way to prevent translation invalidation for oxford comma specifically, we do enforce it but it's a minor detail when compared with actual grammar or spelling errors\r\n\r\nBut aside from that this is not an appropriate first contribution per [our guidelines](https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/pull_requests/pull_request_guidelines.html#no-features-from-new-contributors)\r\n\r\nEdit: To be clear I here refer to refactoring by the dictionary meaning:\r\n> To rewrite existing text in order to improve its readability, reusability or structure without intentionally affecting its meaning. Similar to, but sometimes involving more extensive restructuring than, copy editing. \r\n\r\nAnd that this is not an appropriate new contribution to get contributors familiar with the codebase and workflows\r\n\r\nSo thank you for your contribution, and I look forward to some useful discussion on avoiding issues from changes similar to this, but I will go ahead and close this based on the above\r\n\r\nThank you for your contribution nonetheless and I suggest looking for bugs to fix or more impactful documentation changes!","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5661330287/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":2,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5663001570","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123458#issuecomment-5663001570","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123458","id":5663001570,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABUYqL4g","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-14T11:08:55Z","updated_at":"2026-09-14T11:08:55Z","body":"@DeanLemans I understand that you might disagree with our policy for new contributors, and that's okay, but reacting to maintainers and others enforcing or even informing about this policy is not a constructive way to express your opinion on this, it just creates an unfriendly environment\r\n\r\nPlease consider this in the future and if you wish to protest this feature or other enforcement by maintainers please reach out instead, for example in our [contributors' chat](https://chat.godotengine.org/) and please be mindful of our [code of conduct](https://godotengine.org/code-of-conduct/), thank you and please help keeping this a friendly and welcoming environment!","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5663001570/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]